  "id": "sustained-operations",
  "term": "sustained operations",
  "definition": "Sustained operations are the ongoing mental processes thought to be maintained while a person prepares to retrieve information from memory. In this source, the term refers especially to a proposed common preparatory state, also called retrieval mode, used when getting ready to remember episodic information.",
